  "reason": "The current best is config_031 (scvi_n200 + resnet50 + avgpool + weighted, acc=0.678). The largest single improvement in this study was switching the RNA encoder from PCA to scvi_n200 (~4% gain). The image encoder question remains genuinely unresolved: with pca_n2000, resnet50 (0.639) and imagenet_vit_l (0.635) were nearly tied, leaving it unclear which backbone synergizes better with the richer scvi_n200 representations. Config_037 makes a clean single-variable change (resnet50 → imagenet_vit_l) from the current best, directly testing whether a stronger pretrained image encoder complements scvi_n200's learned latent space. This is the highest-value next experiment because it either identifies a further improvement or confirms resnet50 sufficiency, reducing uncertainty on the image-modality design axis before exploring other dimensions (e.g., transformer aggregation or scgpt)."
}

